From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Schmiedel <martin.schmiedel@tq-group.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] env: tq: k3_common: add ramdisk_addr_r alias

TQ's k3_common.env names the initrd load address "initrd_addr_r", but
U-Boot's generic extlinux boot code expects "ramdisk_addr_r" (see
include/env/ti/ti_common.env). Without it, extlinux.conf boot fails to
load the initrd ("missing environment variable: ramdisk_addr_r").

Add it as an alias at the same address, rather than importing TI's
(which could collide with TQ's own map).

Signed-off-by: Martin Schmiedel <martin.schmiedel@tq-group.com>
---
 include/env/tq/k3_common.env | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/include/env/tq/k3_common.env b/include/env/tq/k3_common.env
--- a/include/env/tq/k3_common.env
+++ b/include/env/tq/k3_common.env
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@ kernel_addr_r=CONFIG_SYS_LOAD_ADDR
 fdt_addr_r=0x8b000000
 fdtoverlay_addr_r=0x8b800000
 initrd_addr_r=0x8c000000
+ramdisk_addr_r=0x8c000000

 /* Offset for spi_flash bootdev */
 script_offset_f=0x7f0000
